# B17: Read/Write Split & `E0502`-Free Nested Method Calls (`StructFieldSplitMut`)

This module demonstrates how Stage 2 (`Jenny-Mem v0.3`) **tri-state parameter boundaries (default read-only `self` vs in-place mutable `mut self`) and evaluation order normalization** eliminate Rust's classic false-positive `E0502 (cannot borrow *self as mutable because it is also borrowed as immutable)` deadlock:
1. **`MotionController`**: Tracks `position: i64 = 0`, `base_step: i64 = 10`, `max_limit: i64 = 1000`, and `ticks: i32 = 0`.
2. **`effective_delta(self, scale: i64)`**: Default read-only borrow; computes `self.base_step * scale`.
3. **`apply_step(mut self, delta: i64)`**: In-place mutable `mut self`; increments `self.ticks += 1`, computes `val next_pos = self.position + delta`, clamps `self.position` to `self.max_limit` if `next_pos > self.max_limit` (else `next_pos`), and returns the updated `self.position`.
4. **`tick_with_scale(mut self, scale: i64)`**: Directly writes the nested call `return self.apply_step(self.effective_delta(scale))` (the compiler automatically evaluates the inner read-only `self.effective_delta(scale)` before invoking the outer `mut self.apply_step(...)`, with zero `E0502` conflict).

```jenny
module field_split_mut

pub struct MotionController {
    pub position: i64 = 0,
    pub base_step: i64 = 10,
    pub max_limit: i64 = 1000,
    pub ticks: i32 = 0,
    invariant self.max_limit > 0
    invariant self.position <= self.max_limit
}

impl MotionController {
    pub fn new(base_step: i64, max_limit: i64) -> MotionController
        requires base_step > 0 && max_limit > 0
        ensures result.position == 0 && result.ticks == 0

    pub fn effective_delta(self, scale: i64) -> i64
        ensures result == self.base_step * scale

    pub fn apply_step(mut self, delta: i64) -> i64
        ensures self.ticks == old(self.ticks) + 1
        ensures result == self.position

    pub fn tick_with_scale(mut self, scale: i64) -> i64
        ensures self.ticks == old(self.ticks) + 1
        ensures result == self.position
}

@example("EX-B17-01: nested mut self + read-only self call without E0502 borrow deadlock") {
    var ctrl = MotionController.new(15, 100)
    val p1 = ctrl.tick_with_scale(3)
    assert(p1 == 45)
    assert(ctrl.ticks == 1)

    val p2 = ctrl.tick_with_scale(5)
    assert(p2 == 100)
    assert(ctrl.ticks == 2)
}
```
